endpoints.response_shape:
Array of EnhancedTransaction (from the official OpenAPI): description (string), type (TransactionType, e.g. 'SWAP','TRANSFER','BUY','SELL'), source (TransactionSource, e.g. 'JUPITER','RAYDIUM','ORCA','PUMP_AMM'; PUMP_FUN appears in API output historically but not in the current doc enum), fee (int lamports), feePayer, signature, slot, timestamp (int UNIX s).
- nativeTransfers[] {fromUserAccount, toUserAccount, amount (int lamports)}
- tokenTransfers[] {fromUserAccount, toUserAccount, fromTokenAccount, toTokenAccount, tokenAmount (NUMBER, DECIMAL-ADJUSTED), mint, tokenStandard}
- accountData[] {account, nativeBalanceChange (lamports), tokenBalanceChanges[] {userAccount, tokenAccount, mint, rawTokenAmount {tokenAmount (STRING raw, signed), decimals}}}
- transactionError {error} | null
- instructions[] {accounts[], data, programId, innerInstructions[] {accounts[], data, programId}}
- events.swap {nativeInput {account, amount (STRING lamports)}, nativeOutput {account, amount}, tokenInputs[] / tokenOutputs[] / tokenFees[] {userAccount, tokenAccount, mint, rawTokenAmount {tokenAmount (raw string), decimals}}, nativeFees[] {account, amount}, innerSwaps[] {tokenInputs[], tokenOutputs[], tokenFees[] (TokenTransfer shape, decimal tokenAmount), nativeFees[], programInfo {source, account, programName, instructionName}}}
- events.nft, events.compressed, events.setAuthority
According to the webhook transaction-type map, PUMP_AMM trades are typed BUY/SELL, not SWAP, so a type=SWAP filter would miss PumpSwap. No new parsers are being added, so pump.fun BuyV2/SellV2 and v1 txs are UNCERTAIN.
